# 16. BUFFER OVERFLOW REVIEW

A buffer overflow occurs when a program handles more data than the allocated buffer can safely contain.

Concept:

```text
Expected input
      ↓
Fixed-size buffer
      ↓
Too much data
      ↓
Memory corruption
```

Potential consequences include:

- Crash
- Memory corruption
- Control-flow corruption
- Potential code execution in vulnerable conditions

---

# 17. STACK CONCEPT

Simplified:

```text
Higher Memory
+----------------+
| Return Address |
+----------------+
| Saved Frame    |
+----------------+
| Local Buffer   |
+----------------+
Lower Memory
```

A vulnerable memory operation may overwrite adjacent memory.

