# 19. LITTLE-ENDIAN

Little-endian systems commonly store the least significant byte first.

Example concept:

```text
0x12345678
```

Memory representation:

```text
78 56 34 12
```

This is an important exploit-development concept.

---

# 20. OFFSET

An offset identifies how many bytes are required before reaching a particular location in corrupted memory.

Conceptually:

```text
AAAA
BBBB
CCCC
DDDD
...
```

A cyclic pattern helps determine where important control data is reached.

