# 21. EXPLOIT MITIGATIONS

Modern systems include protections such as:

### ASLR

Address Space Layout Randomization.

Makes memory addresses less predictable.

### DEP/NX

Helps prevent execution of code in non-executable memory.

### Stack Canaries

Detect certain stack-based corruption before returning from a function.

### CFG

Control Flow Guard can restrict unexpected control-flow transfers.

Memory:

> **A-D-C-C**

```text
A = ASLR
D = DEP/NX
C = Canary
C = CFG
```

---

# 22. REVERSE SHELL REVIEW

A reverse shell means:

> **The target initiates a connection back to the listener.**

Concept:

```text
TARGET
   │
   │ outbound connection
   ▼
LISTENER
```

---

# 23. REVERSE VS BIND SHELL

| Reverse Shell | Bind Shell |
|---|---|
| Target connects outward | Target listens |
| Tester runs listener | Tester connects to target |
| Target initiates | Tester initiates |

Memory:

> **Reverse = Target Calls Back**

> **Bind = Target Waits**

